## Interface: 120100
## Title: Crosshairs
## Notes: Draws a crosshair at the center of the screen and a cursor circle that tracks cast and global cooldown progress
## Author: Tharavol, Claude, GitHub Copilot
## Version: @project-version@
## X-License: GPL-3.0
## SavedVariables: CrosshairsDB

## X-ReleaseNotes: Draws a cross at the centre of the screen and a circle around your cursor that brightens clockwise to track cast and global cooldown progress; hold Alt to expand the circle. The cross and the circle each have independent in-combat and out-of-combat visibility toggles, so you can show them only while fighting, only while idle, both, or neither. Cross leg length and thickness, circle base radius, segment count (8-256, higher is smoother) and segment thickness, and the colour of each element are all configurable from either the options panel or the command line; values typed at the command line are clamped to the supported range and rounded to whole numbers, and the command tells you when it adjusts one. /crosshairs off hides both elements until /crosshairs on restores them, /crosshairs status prints every current setting, and /crosshairs debug on adds a cursor debug dot with diagnostic logging. Configure under Options > AddOns > Crosshairs or with /crosshairs options (alias /ch). Source, issues and release notes: https://github.com/Tharavol/Crosshairs

